  "problem": "**Complementary angles** are two angles whose measures have a sum of $90^\\circ,$ a right angle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14186058/assets/2723049c087f5fa7b061bc9f1d4fb8c894c1e94aee3dfb994a237cd889a377e0.png)\n\nFor example, the angles in the diagram above are complementary because the sum of their measures is $90^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n60^\\circ +30^\\circ = 90^\\circ\n$$",
